          ":question/id": "641fc75f-8c1c-588f-b1c6-9dde40645507",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1714",
          ":question/problem": "What is $\\cos \\left(x + \\frac{π}{3}\\right)$?"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186233455,
          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "609d2236-8468-565e-9ebe-8fd019ac095c",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141380",
          ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{cos}v-\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot 0-\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186234046,
          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
          },
          ":question/id": "11214dee-7d32-5b34-bc7e-86bbedbaab36",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-43384",
          ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{cos}v+\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}x-\\operatorname{cos}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
