          ":question/id": "8e2c5aed-c37a-55b2-85b1-5c5820fa0a08",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119485",
          ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=w$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(w-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡w\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡w\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡w\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡w\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡w-\\operatorname{cos}⁡w).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
