          ":question/id": "273cf5d2-8279-56b4-b179-bc318d5590ca",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141383",
          ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
