          ":question/id": "bedf2d85-2b35-59e9-bfbf-70576d25817c",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141386",
          ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall  the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186292741,
          ":question/answer-fields": [
