          ":question/id": "e50bbccc-38f5-586c-b552-2dd92be5a0c5",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-274501",
          ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ or $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=$\n{{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
