          ":question/id": "57f3ba7e-3790-56b3-8802-fa589493ec0c",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332528",
          ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right)$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right)=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
